import ../../helpers/driver.dl

appearance wide scene appearance:
    maximum width is 320
    padding is 10
    aspect ratio is 16 by 9
    when viewport is below 400:
        aspect ratio is 1 by 1

appearance fixed scene appearance:
    use wide scene appearance
    height is 120

document aspect test:
    surface "Scene" using wide scene appearance
    picture "Preview" from "preview.webp" using wide scene appearance
    surface "Fixed scene" using fixed scene appearance

set instance to an instance of aspect test
to leave aspect surface unchanged {a pointer to UI canvas frame:painting}:
    ignore painting
bind (the control labeled "Scene" in (the address of instance)) in (the address of instance) to (the function named "leave aspect surface unchanged $") for event 1
bind (the control labeled "Fixed scene" in (the address of instance)) in (the address of instance) to (the function named "leave aspect surface unchanged $") for event 1
set view to a UI view of (the address of instance) sized 500 by 600 using font "regular" with the test UI driver
require condition (view's layout's first's bounds' height = 188.75) reporting "A surface did not derive its height from its content aspect ratio"
require condition (view's layout's first's next's bounds' height = 188.75) reporting "A loading image did not reserve its declared aspect ratio"
require condition (view's layout's first's next's next's bounds' height = 120.0) reporting "An aspect ratio overrode an explicit height"
set image to UI image from "preview.webp" in (the address of view)
ignore update UI view the address of view
complete UI image image in (the address of view) with resource (7 as a pointer) sized 400 by 200 at status 1
reflow the UI document in (the address of view)
require condition (view's layout's first's next's bounds' height = 188.75) reporting "Decoded dimensions overrode the declared aspect ratio"
set view's width to 350
reflow the UI document in (the address of view)
require condition (view's layout's first's bounds' height = 320.0) reporting "Responsive aspect ratio rules were not applied"
close the address of view
close the address of instance
print line "Surface and picture aspect ratios respond to the viewport and respect explicit height."
